# The HBM state stream's bandwidth model over K device-memory masters (foldsim --stream-masters, --stream-master-bits,
# --stream-move-bits, --pp-chunk-min-columns; a32-S30: 8 vNoC MEM masters by default, up to 64 direct HBM ports).
# The model prices each master's share (II_bw), a row transfer at least a master's beat; with K, each controller gets
# a master, the heaviest first on the least loaded (foldsim_sim.json `master`, FOLDSIM_VMEM_[G]<k>_MASTER), which the
# kernel's binding (flow/v80/vmem_ports.py) follows.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/Inputs/paged
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/d --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --page-engines 4 --page-engines-pp Leaf > %t/d.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEF < %t/d.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOVH < %t/d/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/k --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --page-engines 4 --page-engines-pp --stream-masters 3 --stream-master-bits 160 --stream-move-bits 256 --pp-chunk-min-columns 1 Leaf > %t/k.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=K < %t/k.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KVH < %t/k/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/flow/v80/vmem_ports.py --sim-vh %t/k/foldsim_sim.vh --mem-ports 1 --masters | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KM

# DEF: state-stream: II_sched 26, HBM state bits a frame 4096 (busiest master 4096), II_bw 4 (8 masters, 8192 b/hc usable)
# NOVH-NOT: _MASTER
# (A 216-bit row moves a 256-bit beat: 3 one-column chunks would move 3 beats, so the class keeps one chunk.)
# K: state-stream: II_sched 26, HBM state bits a frame 8192 (busiest master 8192), II_bw 52 (3 masters, 480 b/hc usable)
# K: foldsim: --stream-masters 3: 1 controllers, bits a frame on the busiest master 8192
# KVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_STREAM_MASTERS 3
# KVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_MASTER 0
# KM: 2

# --stream-stripe 2: a controller's rows over 2 masters (row index mod 2, foldsim_vmem_stripe); the model spreads each
# chunk's bits over them, and the controller lists its 2 masters, the least loaded.
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/s --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --page-engines 4 --page-engines-pp --stream-masters 3 --stream-master-bits 160 --stream-move-bits 256 --stream-stripe 2 Leaf > %t/s.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=S < %t/s.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SVH < %t/s/foldsim_sim.vh
# S: state-stream: II_sched 26, HBM state bits a frame 8192 (busiest master 4096), II_bw 26 (3 masters, stripe 2, 480 b/hc usable)
# S: foldsim: --stream-masters 3: 1 controllers, bits a frame on the busiest master 4096
# SVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_STREAM_STRIPE 2
# SVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_MASTER 0
# SVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_MASTERS 0, 1

# --hbm-round-trip: the reads a controller keeps in flight, by Little's law (the busiest page engine's reads a host
# cycle, 16 a frame of II 26 here, x the round trip + 1/4, a power of two): FOLDSIM_VMEM_OUTSTANDING, the kernel's
# VMEM_OUTSTANDING. A constant of the round trip, not of the instance count.
# RUN: env FOLDSIM_PP_ROWS=balanced foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/o --static --state-in-ram Leaf::4 --state-in-ram-pp --state-scratch-bits 0 --page-engines 4 --page-engines-pp --hbm-round-trip 800 Leaf > %t/o.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=O < %t/o.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVH < %t/o/foldsim_sim.vh
# O: foldsim: --hbm-round-trip 800: {{[0-9]+}} reads in flight a controller (Little: {{[0-9.]+}} reads a host cycle x 800, + 1/4)
# OVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_OUTSTANDING {{(1024|512|2048)}}
